{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7KfWua9MczRykBL7SYW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the letter around the claim your facts can carry. Pharmacies are already losing money on plan prescriptions. Two of the 38 say they'll stop filling them. In 14 counties, losing the local independent means a 20-mile trip.\n\n<final_document>\n**An open letter to the State Employees' Health Plan**\n**From 38 independent pharmacies, about the July 1 pharmacy contract**\n\nSince January, the State Employees' Health Plan has paid our pharmacies less than it costs us to fill your members' prescriptions. For the 20 generic drugs we fill most often, the plan pays us on average $1.80 less per prescription than our cost.\n\nThat is not a small corner of our business. Plan members account for about 22% of the prescriptions filled at our 38 pharmacies, so more than one prescription in five is a state employee or a family member. Some of us make up part of the loss on brand-name drugs. That covers only part of it, and it doesn't explain why a state plan should pay below cost for the generics we fill most.\n\nThis matters most to your members outside the cities. In 14 counties, the nearest pharmacy for most people is an independent one. For most people there, the nearest chain pharmacy is more than 20 miles away. Nine independent pharmacies in this state have closed in the past two years. We don't know how many of them closed because of rates. We do know that two of the 38 pharmacies signing this letter say they'll stop filling prescriptions for plan members if nothing changes. When a pharmacy in one of those counties stops, a state employee who needs a refill has a 40-mile round trip or a mail-order wait.\n\nThe plan can fix this, and the date to do it is coming up. Your contract with your pharmacy benefit manager renews on July 1. We ask that the renewed contract require pharmacies to be paid at least what the drug costs them, plus a fee for filling the prescription.\n\nYou don't have to take our word for the numbers. We will give your staff our purchase invoices for all 20 drugs so you can check our costs against what the plan pays. I'll meet with your staff any time before May 1, early enough for whatever you learn to go into the contract.\n\nWe want to keep filling prescriptions for state employees. We've done it for years, in towns where we are often the only pharmacy. We are asking the plan to make sure that in the July 1 contract, filling a prescription doesn't cost us more than we're paid for it.\n\nTom Reilly\nOwner, Reilly Drug, Carver\nOn behalf of the Main Street Pharmacy Alliance, 38 independent pharmacies\nContact: [phone] · [email]\n</final_document>\n\nBefore you send it:\n\n- **The $1.80.** The letter says \"less than our cost\" because you don't know whether that figure includes the cost of filling. Please check this before May 1, since the plan will see the invoices. If the $1.80 compares the plan's payment to the drug price alone, your real loss per prescription is larger, and you can say so.\n- **Fill in the brackets.** Add your phone and email. If you can find out who heads the plan, add a \"To:\" line with their name.\n- **Two things would strengthen it, if you can get them:** the names of a few of the 14 counties, and whether anyone in the group has raised these rates with the plan before. If someone has, the plan will remember it, so one sentence about it (\"we raised this with the plan in March\") is worth adding.\n- I didn't use the $5,600 figure for your pharmacy, and I didn't say how many pharmacies will close. Your facts don't support either one yet."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1654,"cache_read_input_tokens":10191,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1654},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dd9a43ea-53b3-4daf-bffc-aad29858e87f","uuid":"b074e61d-52fe-4d75-acf5-be4e7d0410d8","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:33:09.423Z","request_id":"req_011Ch7KfWku45zVYfXNEjY6F"}
